COMMAND EXPLANATION
===================

Command:
nohup bash /alert/update_loki_ip.sh >> /var/log/loki_updater.log 2>&1 &


WORD BY WORD BREAKDOWN
----------------------

1. nohup
   ------
   Full form : "No Hang Up"
   Meaning   : Normally when you close your terminal or logout, all
               processes started from that terminal get killed.
               nohup prevents that from happening.
               The script keeps running even after you close SSH session
               or log out of the server.

2. bash /alert/update_loki_ip.sh
   --------------------------------
   Meaning   : Simply runs the script using bash shell.
               bash    = the shell used to execute the script
               /alert/update_loki_ip.sh = full path of the script

3. >>
   ---
   Meaning   : Append output to a file.
               >> adds new output to the END of the file.
               Old logs are NOT deleted.
               If you used > instead of >> it would overwrite
               and delete all old logs every time script runs.

4. /var/log/loki_updater.log
   --------------------------
   Meaning   : This is the log file where all output gets saved.
               Every log(), echo, print statement from the script
               gets written into this file.
               You can read it anytime using:
               tail -f /var/log/loki_updater.log

5. 2>&1
   -----
   Meaning   : Redirect error output to same place as normal output.
               2  = error output (stderr)
               1  = normal output (stdout)
               2>&1 means send errors to same destination as normal output.
               Without this, error messages would be lost and not
               saved in the log file. With this, both normal logs
               AND errors go into the same log file.

6. &
   --
   Meaning   : Run the script in the background.
               Without & your terminal would be stuck/blocked
               until the script finishes (which is never because
               the script runs forever in a while true loop).
               With & the script runs in background and your
               terminal is immediately free to use.


FULL COMMAND SUMMARY
--------------------

   nohup                          = don't kill when terminal closes
   bash /alert/update_loki_ip.sh  = run this script
   >>                             = append (don't overwrite) logs
   /var/log/loki_updater.log      = save output to this log file
   2>&1                           = save errors to same log file
   &                              = run in background


IMPORTANT NOTE
--------------
In your current setup the script is managed by systemd service
(loki-ip-updater.service) which handles all of this automatically.

You should NOT run the nohup command anymore.
Running it will create a DUPLICATE instance of the script.

Always use systemctl commands instead:

   Start   : systemctl start loki-ip-updater.service
   Stop    : systemctl stop loki-ip-updater.service
   Restart : systemctl restart loki-ip-updater.service
   Status  : systemctl status loki-ip-updater.service
   Logs    : tail -f /var/log/loki_updater.log
